cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "nice-prisma, a service-friendly toolkit for PRISMA-based literature surveys"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below, together with the original toolkit listed under references."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Christian"
    family-names: "Schuler"
    email: "christianschuler8989@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Saarland University & DFKI"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2686-6350"
repository-code: "https://github.com/christianschuler8989/nice-prisma"
url: "https://github.com/christianschuler8989/nice-prisma"
abstract: >
  nice-prisma is a Python toolkit for PRISMA 2020 literature surveys. It
  covers polite corpus ingestion from OpenAlex with a local page cache,
  cross-source deduplication, stable document identity and tracking across
  all survey stages, title-abstract screening, full-text extraction with
  PyMuPDF, MMAT 2018 quality assessment, PRISMA 2020 flow diagrams, and
  bibliometric analysis. It is a fork of the PRISMA toolkit by Proportione.
keywords:
  - systematic literature review
  - PRISMA 2020
  - MMAT 2018
  - OpenAlex
  - bibliometrics
  - research synthesis
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
